%table
  %thead
    %tr
      %th.table-title{colspan: 2} Moiety Explorer
    %tr
      %td.even.padding-10{colspan: 2}
        Every author's moiety on an HSLuv color wheel: hue runs around the circle and saturation runs outward, with the
        slider setting the wheel's lightness. HSLuv spaces colors evenly to the eye, so two moieties close together
        here also look close together on the page. Dots near the wheel's lightness are drawn solid, the rest faded.
        Click the wheel or enter a hex code to find the nearest moieties.
        = link_to 'List by color', users_path(sort: 'moiety')
  %tbody
    %tr
      %td.odd.padding-10.vtop.centered.moiety-wheel-cell
        %noscript The moiety explorer needs JavaScript.
        .moiety-wheel-wrapper
          %canvas#moiety-wheel{width: 400, height: 400}
          #moiety-hover
        %br
        = label_tag :moiety_lightness, 'Lightness'
        %input#moiety_lightness{type: 'range', min: 0, max: 100, step: 1, value: 60}
        %span#moiety-lightness-value 60
      %td.odd.padding-10.vtop.moiety-wheel-cell
        = label_tag :moiety_hex, 'Hex code'
        \#
        = text_field_tag :moiety_hex, nil, maxlength: 6, style: 'width: 80px;', placeholder: 'Hex code'
        %span#moiety-swatch
        #moiety-sample.hidden
          %span#moiety-sample-name= current_user&.username || 'Your Name'
          %br
          %span#moiety-hsluv
        %table#moiety-nearest.hidden
          %thead
            %tr
              %th.sub{colspan: 4} Nearest moieties
            %tr
              %th.sub.centered Moiety
              %th.sub Name
              %th.sub Hex
              %th.sub{title: 'Perceptual color difference (CIELUV ΔE): 0 is identical'} Distance
          %tbody
